<Doc
  title="Send an iPhone video on Discord | Sub20"
  description="iPhone videos are often over Discord's limit, recorded in HEVC that not every device plays, and in HDR. How to send one that plays, in ordinary colour."
  current="guides"
  heading="Send an iPhone video on Discord"
  lead="An iPhone video has three things against it on Discord: it is big, it is usually HEVC, which some devices won't play in the chat, and newer iPhones record it in HDR. Converting it to H.264 in ordinary colour, at a size under the limit, fixes all three."
>
  <h2>Why it doesn't just send</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Size.</b> A minute of 4K video is hundreds of megabytes; Discord's free limit is 20 MB.</li>
    <li><b>HEVC.</b> With <b>High Efficiency</b> chosen in Settings, Camera, Formats (the default), the iPhone records HEVC. Discord plays HEVC only on devices that can decode it, so on older computers people have to download the file to watch it. See <a href={u("guides/hevc/")}>why HEVC may not play</a>.</li>
    <li><b>HDR.</b> iPhone 12 and later record HDR video by default. Converted without care, HDR comes out grey and washed out.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Send it from a computer</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Move the video to your computer (AirDrop on a Mac, or the Photos app or a cable on Windows).</li>
    <li>Drop it on <a href={u("download/")}>Sub20</a> and drag the yellow handles to the part worth sending.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Compress</b>. Sub20 encodes H.264, converts HDR to ordinary colour (the stage says when a video was HDR), and keeps a portrait video upright.</li>
    <li>Press Ctrl+C (⌘C on a Mac) and paste into Discord.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Send it from the phone</h2>
  <p><a href={u("app/")}>Sub20 Lite</a> is the same app in a browser, and nothing is uploaded. It encodes H.264 at the size you pick, and on a phone <b>Share</b> hands the result to the Discord app.</p>
  <p>Lite converts HDR to ordinary colour too, through the browser, so the colours come out right but a little darker than the desktop app makes them.</p>

  <h2>Record it ready to send</h2>
  <p>If you send a lot of phone videos, two settings make them easier:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Settings, Camera, Formats: <b>Most Compatible</b> records H.264, which Discord plays.</li>
    <li>Settings, Camera, Record Video: <b>HDR Video</b> off records ordinary colour.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The video still has to fit under the limit, so a long one still needs trimming and compressing.</p>
</Doc>
